  "details": "Just to be clear up front: this is NOT requesting to grab a *single* handful of *successively descending* children (like multiple links of a long tail).  That might be neat but is a different issue.\n\nThis issue is about trying to cut down on physbone components by using the same component for BOTH halves of a symmetrical pair of physbones (i.e ears), which works great, EXCEPT that someone trying to grab both ears SIMULTANEOUSLY in both hands won't be able to.\n\nThis is discussed here: https://www.reddit.com/r/VRchat/comments/z2yfqh/a_tip_for_optimizing_physbones/ The good news is the main post (how a root bone containing both symmetric bones can save on components) and the bad news is in the first reply (how doing so will prevent both-hand grabbing).\n\nThis is the only shortcoming with an approach that's otherwise perfect for cutting down on physbone component count on Quest.  And it seems like it might simply be an oversight, rather than some kind of optimization, since after all, physics ARE still running for all of the physbones involved, and both of the user's hands CAN still grab *other* physbones simultaneously, so I don't think adding this capability would come at any kind of meaningful performance cost?  (I almost filed this as a bug rather than a feature request, in fact...)",
